From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 21:05:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos: google: gs201-cheetah: charger limits and
 a sink-only port

Give the battery the charger limits the MAX77759 charger programs at
probe, and point pmic@66 (whose charger cell uses the parent's node) at
it. Without them the charger driver falls back to 4.3 V and 2.27 A.

 - Float voltage 4.45 V: stock's google,fv-max-uv and the top of its
   google,chg-cv-limits.
 - Fast charge current 1.47 A: 0.3 C of the 4926 mAh pack, the lowest
   google,chg-cc-limits entry (in percent of capacity) at any voltage
   tier between 10 and 46 degC, since there is no step charging here.

Describe the still disabled Type-C port as sink only. On this board
VBUS is sourced from an external boost (stock: max77759,ext-otg-only)
that has no driver, so there is nothing to put in vbus-supply and a dual
role port would fail every attempt to become source. Drop the source
PDO and try-power-role until that exists.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-cheetah.dts  | 39 ++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 25 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-cheetah.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-cheetah.dts
index 50737a8d8..42b7317fc 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-cheetah.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-cheetah.dts
@@ -59,6 +59,15 @@ battery: battery {
 		/* Google's fv-max-uv; VEmpty of the gauge model */
 		voltage-max-design-microvolt = <4450000>;
 		voltage-min-design-microvolt = <3300000>;
+		/*
+		 * Charger limits without Google's step charging: the float
+		 * voltage is fv-max-uv, the top of google,chg-cv-limits
+		 * (4.2/4.3/4.45 V). The fast charge current is 0.3 C, the
+		 * lowest google,chg-cc-limits entry at any voltage tier from
+		 * 10 to 46 degC, and a charger selector (0x16) exactly.
+		 */
+		constant-charge-voltage-max-microvolt = <4450000>;
+		constant-charge-current-max-microamp = <1466730>;
 	};
 
 	gpio-keys {
@@ -322,10 +331,12 @@ &ufs_0_phy {
  *
  * The Type-C port controller stays disabled: the USB link is our only way
  * into the phone, and TCPM would take over VBUS and data role from the
- * forced-VBUS setup the USB PHY uses today. The charger has no DT node of
- * its own (it is an MFD cell of pmic@66); note that its probe turns
- * charging off until a "tcpm-source" power supply reports a source, so do
- * not load it before the Type-C side works.
+ * forced-VBUS setup the USB PHY uses today. Its graph links to the USB PHY
+ * (orientation, i.e. VBUS valid) and dwc3 (role switch) are added by the
+ * bring-up overlays. The charger has no DT node of its own (it is an MFD
+ * cell of pmic@66, which carries its monitored-battery); its probe turns
+ * charging off until a "tcpm-source" power supply reports a source, unless
+ * it is loaded with default_ilim_ua.
  */
 &usi13 {
 	samsung,mode = <USI_MODE_I2C>;
@@ -345,23 +356,21 @@ usb-typec@25 {
 		status = "disabled";
 
 		/*
-		 * Power roles and PDOs as on gs101 (the same MAX77759 design).
-		 * PD stays off, and the orientation/role-switch ports to the
-		 * USB PHY and dwc3 come with the Type-C work.
+		 * Sink only for now: sourcing VBUS goes through an external
+		 * boost on this board (stock: max77759,ext-otg-only, switched
+		 * by MAX77759 GPIO5 "bst-on" and the TCPC's EXTBST_CTRL), which
+		 * has no driver yet, so there is no vbus-supply. MAX77759 GPIO6
+		 * is the VBUS input switch (stock in-switch-gpio): leave it.
+		 * Stock is dual role with try-sink and a 5 V / 900 mA source
+		 * PDO. Sink PDOs as on gs101 and stock; PD stays off.
 		 */
 		connector {
 			compatible = "usb-c-connector";
 			label = "USB-C";
 			data-role = "dual";
-			power-role = "dual";
+			power-role = "sink";
 			self-powered;
-			try-power-role = "sink";
 			op-sink-microwatt = <2600000>;
-			source-pdos = <PDO_FIXED(5000, 900,
-						 (PDO_FIXED_SUSPEND
-						  | PDO_FIXED_USB_COMM
-						  | PDO_FIXED_DATA_SWAP
-						  | PDO_FIXED_DUAL_ROLE))>;
 			sink-pdos = <PDO_FIXED(5000, 3000,
 					       (PDO_FIXED_DATA_SWAP
 						| PDO_FIXED_USB_COMM
@@ -440,6 +449,8 @@ pmic@66 {
 		pinctrl-names = "default";
 		interrupt-controller;
 		#interrupt-cells = <2>;
+		/* for the charger cell */
+		monitored-battery = <&battery>;
 
 		gpio {
 			compatible = "maxim,max77759-gpio";
